{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>When a man steals.</b> The slaughterer and the seller are also included, as it is written ״אם ימצא הגנב״ etc. And this section was stated to take him out of the general rule, to obligate him in payment of four and five." "<b>Or slaughters it or sells it.</b> If the slaughterer is liable, the seller — no need to say. And if you ask: this is not an argument a fortiori unless you penalize from the law; therefore it says ומכרו to teach you that we do not penalize from the law." "<b>Or slaughters it or sells it.</b> Just as slaughter is something that does not return, so too sale is something that does not return." "<b>Five cattle, and four sheep</b> etc. Because the thief treated himself more lightly with a sheep than with an ox, since he carried it on his shoulder when he stole it, and further that he did no labor with it as with an ox, Scripture was lenient in its payment more than for an ox. Another interpretation: it is just that one who steals an ox should pay more than one who steals a sheep, for if he were not practiced in theft he could not steal so large an animal, but one who steals a sheep has an opening to say: I could not, I am not accustomed to the craft of theft — four sheep suffice. Another interpretation: it is just that one who steals an ox should pay extra payment more than one who steals sheep, because he caused damage to the owner of the ox, who used to plow with it, which is not so with sheep." "<b>In place of the ox, in place of the sheep.</b> Scripture repeated this to tell you that the law of four and five applies only to an ox and a sheep alone."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {1 "א״כ resolved as אם כן ('if so'); כ״‎ש as כל שכן ('all the more so').", 4 "שנאן is obscure; read hyper-literally as written. Likely a corruption of שנאם ('it repeated them'), the nun possibly a copyist's error for a mem."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:45.597017055Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}